    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "La Lagunilla was founded in the 16th century during Mexico’s colonial era, making it one of the city’s oldest neighborhoods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tastetimetraveler.blogspot.com/2024/02/exploring-la-lagunilla-neighborhood.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally home to Otomi people, the area evolved into a bustling commercial hub in colonial times, famous for its flea market.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tastetimetraveler.blogspot.com/2024/02/exploring-la-lagunilla-neighborhood.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Today, La Lagunilla remains a vibrant cultural center where Mexican traditions blend in colorful street markets and artisan stalls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tastetimetraveler.blogspot.com/2024/02/exploring-la-lagunilla-neighborhood.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On Sundays, the antique market lights up with collectors and art lovers, offering furniture, books, and folk art from across the country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tastetimetraveler.blogspot.com/2024/02/exploring-la-lagunilla-neighborhood.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The neighborhood is easily reached by metro at Garibaldi‑Lagunilla station or by the Metrobús Line 7, which opened in March 2018.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://tastetimetraveler.blogspot.com/2024/02/exploring-la-lagunilla-neighborhood.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "La Lagunilla’s historic center sits just a short walk from the Zócalo, placing it at the heart of Mexico City’s cultural life.",
